---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Website Support &amp; Maintenance | Kelp Agency"
  description="Keep your website stable and useful with updates, fixes, broken-link cleanup, content support, and ongoing improvements."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Ongoing Support Services"
    title="Website Support"
    description="A website that never gets attention eventually turns into a liability. We provide ongoing support that keeps sites updated, stable, and usable after launch."
    lottieFile="website-support.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Most websites do not break all at once. They slowly drift. Plugins fall
        behind, forms stop working, content gets stale, links break, and no one
        has a clear plan for keeping the site healthy.
      </p>
      <p>
        By the time someone notices, the site is already creating friction for
        visitors and extra stress for the team.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We handle the ongoing maintenance that keeps a website usable and
        trustworthy: updates, backups, bug fixes, broken-link cleanup, and
        monitoring for issues that should be caught before they become bigger
        problems.
      </p>
      <h2>Catch the Small Failures Before They Compound</h2>
      <p>
        Support can include platform updates, backups, bug fixes, broken links,
        form checks, content changes, and performance or usability improvements.
        We prioritize by business impact: a broken booking path matters more
        than a minor visual inconsistency on a rarely visited page.
      </p>
      <h2>Improve, Not Just Maintain</h2>
      <p>
        The best support rhythm makes room for new evidence. We can review
        customer questions, search visibility, and conversion paths alongside
        technical health. Kelp's free{" "}
        <a href="/website-checker/">Website Checker</a> offers a quick first
        report on broken links, AI search readiness, technical and local SEO,
        schema, and conversion opportunities. Talk with Kelp about a support
        plan.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        Support includes more than applying updates. A form failure can stop
        enquiries, a broken product rule can disrupt orders, and a content
        change can create an unclear customer path. We prioritize issues by
        their effect on visitors and staff, document the fix, and look for the
        pattern behind repeat problems. That gives the site a practical path
        from repair to improvement.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Maintenance and update schedule</li>
        <li>Bug and broken-path triage</li>
        <li>Content and usability improvements</li>
        <li>Regular review of site health and priorities</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        We begin with the platform, access, current issue list, and the paths
        customers use most. A quick{" "}
        <a href="/website-checker/">Website Checker</a> report can help surface
        issues, then we define the support level the site needs.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Can Kelp support a site it did not build?</h3>
      <p>
        Potentially. We first review the platform, codebase, hosting, and access
        so the scope and responsibilities are clear.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Support Needs
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={82} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
